<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Radiothermal.xml                   UtinniPatches - COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `wasteland:radiothermal-solitary-living-furnace-spacing-law`
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/wasteland.md §4: "The radiothermal
  solitaries — so hot with their own decay they must dump heat to live:
  they haunt the cold dark scour and keep distance from their own kind or
  cook each other (the spacing law returns, driven by heat). A warm boulder
  in the black country means one passed; a tamed one is a living furnace
  that heats a shelter all winter and irradiates it the entire time."
  roster's own `new_defs` entry, rosters/wasteland.json, mechanic_load "NEW
  C#: heat emission + spacing").

  Checked cast_assignment.csv/animal_census.csv first (per this item's own
  "watch out") for any donor that already emits ambient heat as a creature
  mechanic — none found; the roster's own mechanic_load line agrees ("no
  donor emits heat"). No RimSage available from this machine (WSL/Mac,
  CLAUDE.md's own standing note) to verify whether CompHeatPusher (the
  vanilla building-heater comp) attaches cleanly to a Pawn ThingDef, so that
  is NOT assumed here — ships as a plain interim creature, same "def lands
  first, behaviour comp follows" posture RUT_BrineBattery (this same wave)
  and DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1/CRACKED_LANDS_SEALED_WAKE_MECHANISM_1
  used. Both halves of the mechanic_load (the heat emission AND the
  same-species spacing law that makes "cook each other" a real threat) are
  genuinely new C#, so both stay inside WASTELAND_RADIOTHERMAL_SOLITARY_1
  (already filed by the prior session) rather than being guessed at inline.

  Body: solitary, heavy, ground-hugging quadruped (QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail,
  already used elsewhere in this repo for medium/large solitary creatures) —
  "a living boulder that happens to move" reads as low MoveSpeed + high mass
  + high armor (its own decay-heat has presumably toughened it), not agility.
  roamMtbDays widened well past this mod's herd-animal defaults and
  herdAnimal=false: "solitary" and "keep distance from their own kind" are
  read as real stats (never grouping, rarely encountered) even before the
  spacing-law C# lands, the same "flavor text as a real stat" discipline
  RUT_MortuaryCrawler's manhunter-zeroing used.

  Art: genuinely new, no donor texture fits "cracked, glowing-ember hide"
  (checked infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} for
  "radiothermal"/"living furnace" first — clean). Three facing jobs filed
  this pass (south/east/north; west mirrors east) — rutradiothermal_v1_
  {south,east,north}.json, provenance WASTELAND_RADIOTHERMAL_SOLITARY_1.

  WASTELAND_RADIOTHERMAL_SOLITARY_1 closed both halves this item's own
  "Still owed" section named:

  1. Heat emission — "a tamed one is a living furnace that heats a shelter
     all winter." RimSage-verified (RimWorld 1.6 decompile, Source/Verse/
     CompHeatPusher.cs): the vanilla comp reads only Thing-level members
     (SpawnedOrAnyParentSpawned, AmbientTemperature, PositionHeld, MapHeld)
     with no Building-only assumption, so it attaches cleanly to a Pawn
     ThingDef as-is. Wired directly below via CompProperties_HeatPusher,
     compClass pointed at RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.
     RM_CompHeatPusherGated (a thin subclass that adds this kit's mod
     settings gate — ambientHeatPusherEnabled — on top of the same vanilla
     tick/temperature logic Campfire itself uses; numbers calibrated off
     Campfire's own heatPerSecond=21/heatPushMaxTemperature=28).
  2. Same-species spacing law — "keep distance from their own kind or cook
     each other." Genuinely new C#, both halves in
     RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors: RM_JobGiver_AvoidOwnKind (inserted
     globally via RM_ThinkTree_VerminBehaviors, insertTag Animal_PreMain —
     a no-op for every other animal in the game) steers this pawn away from
     the nearest other RUT_Radiothermal once one comes within
     avoidRadiusCells; RM_CompHeatCook (via RM_CompProperties_
     SpeciesSpacingCook below) is the "or cook each other" consequence —
     self-inflicted heat damage every cookIntervalTicks while another
     RUT_Radiothermal is still within the tighter cookRadiusCells (a pen, a
     cage, a cornered map — avoidance is meant to prevent this, not
     guarantee it never happens). Both halves read their tuning from the
     single RM_SpeciesSpacingExtension below.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RUT_Radiothermal</defName>
    <label>radiothermal</label>
    <description>A heavy, ground-hugging animal so hot with its own decay that it must constantly dump the excess or cook from the inside. It moves rarely and alone — two of them sharing ground for long enough is a fire, not a meeting — and the cracked, faintly glowing hide is the reason nothing ever finds it by scent alone. A warm boulder sitting in otherwise dead-cold country usually means one has just moved on.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.6</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>110</Mass>
      <MarketValue>340</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.65</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-40</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>70</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.25</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.2</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.9</ArmorRating_Heat>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>fused claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>14</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>fused claw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>14</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightLeg</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>12</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.4</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>true</predator>
      <maxPreyBodySize>1.4</maxPreyBodySize>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <baseBodySize>2.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>2.4</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.5</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Heavy</leatherDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <wildness>0.65</wildness>
      <roamMtbDays>25</roamMtbDays>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.08</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>22</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>14</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.5, 0.3)</li>
          <li>(2, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.25</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.5</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Warg_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>

    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_HeatPusher">
        <compClass>RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompHeatPusherGated</compClass>
        <heatPerSecond>30</heatPerSecond>
        <heatPushMaxTemperature>24</heatPushMaxTemperature>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_SpeciesSpacingCook" />
    </comps>

    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_SpeciesSpacingExtension">
        <avoidRadiusCells>8</avoidRadiusCells>
        <cookRadiusCells>3</cookRadiusCells>
        <cookDamagePerInterval>4</cookDamagePerInterval>
        <cookIntervalTicks>250</cookIntervalTicks>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RUT_Radiothermal</defName>
    <label>radiothermal</label>
    <labelPlural>radiothermals</labelPlural>
    <race>RUT_Radiothermal</race>
    <combatPower>140</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>1.5</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_Radiothermal/RUT_Radiothermal</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_Radiothermal/RUT_Radiothermal</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.6</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_Radiothermal/RUT_Radiothermal</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>2.0</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
